(footprint "Potentiometer_Alpha_RD902F-40-00D_Dual_Vertical"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Taiwan Alpha RD902F-40-00D, 9 mm vertical DUAL-gang potentiometer - the two-gang sibling of Potentiometer_Alpha_RD901F-40-00D_Single_Vertical, same M7x0.75 bushing and same shaft, so it drops into a panel drilled for the single. Land pattern from the KiCad stock footprint, checked against doc/alpha pots.pdf page 5 (RD902F-40-00D): 6-o1.0 holes as two 3-pin rows of 2.5 pitch, the rows 2.5 apart, front row 7.5 from the shaft; mounting lugs 7.5 from the front pin row and 9.5 apart centre to centre (datasheet 11.3 outer span less 1.8 lug width), lug slots 1.1 x 1.8. NOTE the lug span is 9.5 here against the single's 9.6 - the datasheet really does draw them 0.1 apart, it is not a transcription slip. Pins 1-2-3 are gang R1 (front row, nearest the shaft), pins 4-5-6 are gang R2 (back row); wiper is the centre pin of each, 2 and 5. The two gangs are electrically independent - nothing is commoned inside the part. 3D model is the real dual-gang body, in the same frame as the single's STEP: identical in x (-5.787 to 5.787) and z (-3.5 to 25.0), and extending 2.5 further on the pin side (y -10.150 against the single's -7.650). That 2.5 is the second row's offset arriving independently from the solid model, which is worth knowing because 5 is the easy thing to assume. The single's seating therefore works unchanged: offset 7.5 -2.5 0, rotate 0 0 90.")
	(tags "potentiometer vertical 9mm dual gang alpha rd902f eurorack")
